------------------------------------------------------------
86. VERY IMPORTANT POINTER RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

RULE 1:

Never dereference an uninitialized pointer.

RULE 2:

Never dereference NULL.

RULE 3:

Never use memory after free.

RULE 4:

Do not free the same allocation twice.

RULE 5:

Every successful dynamic allocation needs an ownership plan.

RULE 6:

Do not modify a string literal.

RULE 7:

Do not return the address of a local automatic variable.

RULE 8:

Do not perform pointer arithmetic outside the permitted array
object boundaries.

RULE 9:

A one-past-the-end pointer can be formed but not dereferenced.

RULE 10:

Do not assume all pointers have the same size on every system.

RULE 11:

Do not confuse:

    array
    pointer
    pointer to array
    array of pointers

RULE 12:

Do not assume casting makes an invalid pointer access safe.

